/Title (BRICS+ is the expanded format of BRICS, an influential intergovernmental organization comprising major emerging economies. Originally founded as BRIC in 2009 by Brazil, Russia, India, and China, the group was renamed BRICS in 2010 with the addition of South Africa. In 2024, the bloc underwent significant expansion with the admission of Egypt, Ethiopia, Iran, and the United Arab Emirates, followed by Indonesia in 2025, bringing the total membership to ten countries.)
